[00:26.82]1. Mankind has stumbled for centuries in darkness.
[00:32.78]Vain is their quest as they try to catch the wind.
[00:38.88]Man’s tragic flaw is revealed in its starkness;
[00:44.86]None can they save, for they all have sinned.
[00:56.50](Chorus)
[00:57.50]Sing with good cheer, for God’s Kingdom is here!
[01:02.88]His Son’s mighty reign brings us freedom from fear.
[01:09.58]Through him, at last, evil soon will be past;
[01:14.72]This hope, like an anchor, is holding us fast.
[01:46.38]2. “God’s day is near!” rings the Kingdom proclamation;
[01:52.40]Men will no longer cry out to God: “How long?”
[01:57.64]Soon he will free all his groaning creation.
[02:04.38]Praise God Almighty, and join our song.
[02:17.74](Chorus)
[02:20.22]Sing with good cheer, for God’s Kingdom is here!
[02:26.02]His Son’s mighty reign brings us freedom from fear.
[02:32.26]Through him, at last, evil soon will be past;
[02:37.84]This hope, like an anchor, is holding us fast.
